# `for (const count of counts.values())` walks the table of the map in line. `values()` makes no iterator object, and a step makes no result object.
# CHECK-LABEL: name="total" role=Source
# CHECK: Int64 b@[[table]] = Load(b@[[map]], offset = 16, ControlDependent|Reads:CollectionStorage, {{*}}:CollectionTable)
# CHECK: Patchpoint({{*}}isLoopPoll{{*}}:LoopHint)
# CHECK: Load(b@{{*}}Reads:CollectionEntries, {{*}}:MapNext)
# CHECK: Double b@{{*}} = Add(b@{{*}}, b@{{*}}, {{*}}:Add)
# CHECK-LABEL: end of function
# The patchpoints on the likely paths are the polls of the two copies of the loop: nothing is called and nothing is allocated.
# The function has calls, and Windows passes arguments in other registers: its count is not checked.
# The body touches no collection, so the loop has a copy for a table that stays as it is: the table, its kind, its size and the place of its entries are read ahead of that copy.
# A turn of it polls, compares the position with the size and loads the entry. An entry that was deleted, a table of another kind and the end of the walk leave it.
# FAST-LABEL: steps by 1
# FAST-NOT: Reads:CollectionStorage
# FAST: Patchpoint({{*}}isLoopPoll{{*}}:LoopHint)
# FAST-NOT: Reads:CollectionStorage
# FAST: Load(b@{{*}}Reads:CollectionEntries, {{*}}:MapNext)
# FAST-NOT: Reads:CollectionStorage
# FAST: Load(b@{{*}}Reads:CollectionEntries, {{*}}:MapNext)
# FAST-NOT: Reads:Collection
# FAST-LABEL: end of loop
# X64LOOP: loop #{{*}}, instructions: 13, patchpoints: 1
# ARM64LOOP: loop #{{*}}, instructions: 15, patchpoints: 1
# X64: instructions: 87, patchpoints: 2, rare instructions: 13
# ARM64: instructions: 78, patchpoints: 1, rare instructions: 13
